    "created_at": "2020-01-25T01:35:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-25T01:35:20Z",
    "body": "For the non-bfcache case, I think it would make sense to just use the time the event occurs (similar to what I assume browsers already do today?).\r\n\r\nI consider the bfcache vs. non-bfcache `pageshow` cases to be very similar to a UI event vs. a non-UI event, e.g. `click` vs `DOMContentLoaded`. In the former, browsers can set `event.timeStamp` to the moment when the event occurred (rather than when the listeners run), but in the latter browsers typically run the event listeners as soon as the event occurs.\r\n\r\nFor the bfcache case, I think it would make sense to set the timestamp to when the user clicked the back button/forward button, but in all other cases I think it's fine to use the moment the event listener tasks are queued.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
